 ```
 
+Construct an `Offcanvas` engine over a start-edge `.offcanvas` element with scrolling left
+available, and show it with the button that asked for it: the backdrop fades in beside the slide,
+and focus moves into the element until it hides and returns to the button.
+
+```ts
+import { Offcanvas } from '@orkestrel/veneer/browser'
+
+const button = document.createElement('button')
+const host = document.createElement('div')
+host.className = 'offcanvas offcanvas-start'
+host.tabIndex = -1
+document.body.append(button, host)
+const offcanvas = new Offcanvas(host, { scroll: true })
+const opened = await offcanvas.show(button)
+const closed = await offcanvas.hide()
+offcanvas.destroy()
+```
